{"duration_api_ms":6574,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3a3816e6-f422-4de4-a6cc-cf15e27675df","total_cost_usd":0.0008234,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":876,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":415},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1250,"outputTokens":1114,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":707,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0008234,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":629,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":707,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Sponsor economics**\n- **Breakeven AUM:** Compare expected fee revenue (AUM × net expense ratio) against fixed costs such as audit, legal, fund accounting, index licensing, exchange listing, compliance, and board fees. Estimate the AUM needed to cover these.\n- **Fee waivers and expense caps:** Check how long the sponsor will absorb costs and what happens when the cap expires.\n- **Lineup economics:** Assess whether the sponsor's other funds share overhead and whether a weak fund draws resources from stronger ones.\n\n**Seed capital**\n- **Seed size, source, and duration:** Note whether seed is sponsor-funded or from a third party, and how long it is committed.\n- **Seed-to-flows ratio:** Track how much organic inflow replaces seed. Seed that stays unredeemed for long periods signals weak demand.\n- **Seed concentration:** Watch for a single holder controlling a large share of assets.\n\n**Growth and viability signals**\n- **Net flows versus market returns:** Separate asset growth from inflows.\n- **Distribution access:** Track platform, model, and advisor adoption.\n- **Trading activity:** Monitor volume, spreads, creation/redemption activity, and authorized participant count.\n\n**Closure triggers:** Review the board's minimum-AUM policy and any stated liquidation thresholds.","ttft_ms":3077,"type":"result","duration_ms":5333,"uuid":"b8e88e29-f671-4a2b-ba83-29ad9259b00a","ttft_stream_ms":461,"time_to_request_ms":95,"first_content_frame_ms":461,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
